#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""pcoin-rails-daily -- one message a day about the four rails that matter.

    checker.pc.am   webbuilderbot   aicontrol.pc.am   webai.pc.am

WHY THIS EXISTS. Every existing monitor answers "is it ticking". None answers
"did anything happen, and does it look right". `pcoin-deposit-watch` will report
a rail healthy for a month while it credits nobody, because a rail with no
customers and a rail that has silently stopped crediting look identical from
outside. This tells those apart, and it is what the owner reads in the morning.

THE RULES IT IS BUILT ON, each one from an incident in this estate:

 1. IT POSTS EVERY DAY, INCLUDING A COMPLETELY QUIET ONE. A monitor that only
    speaks when something is wrong cannot be told apart from a monitor that has
    died. The date is in the subject and REPEAT_HOURS=0, so pcoin-notify's
    dedupe can never swallow a day whose numbers match yesterday's.

 2. A RAIL IT COULD NOT READ IS "UNKNOWN", NEVER OMITTED AND NEVER ZERO. The
    deposit watcher once guarded each rail with `if [ -r <config> ]` and no
    else, so on a host where a rail did not live the check did not fail, it
    VANISHED -- and it logged "all healthy" for weeks having examined almost
    nothing. Here an unreadable rail gets a line saying so, and the totals say
    they are a floor rather than a total.

 3. NOTHING UNANSWERABLE BECOMES A NUMBER. "No deposits pending" yields NULL
    for the oldest-pending age, not 0, because 0 reads as "stuck for zero
    hours". "Never credited" yields NULL, not -1. A query that did not run
    prints as a failure, never as zero.

 4. EVERY RAIL REPORTS ITS WATCHER'S OWN HEARTBEAT. Every stuck-money figure
    here is derived from rows THE WATCHER WROTE. If the watcher is dead it
    writes nothing, the pending count is 0, and the report would read perfectly
    healthy while money piled up unseen. The heartbeat is what makes "0 stuck"
    mean something. checker and aicontrol keep it in `settings.pcoin
    .last_poll_at`; webbuilderbot and webai in a rate-cache/heartbeat timestamp.

WHAT IT READS. checker is local to this host. The other three are reached over
SSH with the fleet panel key, running read-only queries. That key already lives
here so this adds no new exposure -- but it is fleet-wide root, so if this ever
moves hosts, give it its own restricted key rather than copying the panel key.

WHAT IT WRITES. One Telegram message through pcoin-notify, and one JSON file per
day under STATE_DIR so the history exists off Telegram and "when did this rail
last credit anything" has an answer that is not a chat search.

    pcoin-rails-daily --dry-run     print the message, send nothing
    pcoin-rails-daily               collect, save, send
"""

